{"name":"Squid Pink","hex":"#f5b4bd","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"squid","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of several carnivorous marine cephalopod mollusks, of the order Teuthida, having a mantle, eight arms, and a pair of tentacles.","A fishhook with a piece of bright lead, bone, or other substance fastened on its shank to imitate a squid."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To fish with a squid fishhook.","To cause squidding (an improper, partial, parachute inflation, that results in the sides of the parachute folding in on the center, and pulsating back and forth)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/squid"},{"term":"pink","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A color reminiscent of pinks, the flowers.","Magenta, the colour evoked by red and blue light when combined."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a colour between red and white; pale red.","Of a fox-hunter's jacket: scarlet."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pink"}],"entries":[{"title":"Squid","blocks":[{"text":"A squid is a mollusc with an elongated soft body, large eyes, eight arms, and two tentacles in the orders Myopsida, Oegopsida, and Bathyteuthida. Like all other cephalopods, squid have a distinct head, bilateral symmetry, and a mantle. They are mainly soft-bodied, like octopuses, but have a small internal skeleton in the form of a rod-like gladius or pen, made of chitin."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Sepioteuthis_sepioidea_%28Caribbean_Reef_Squid%29.jpg/330px-Sepioteuthis_sepioidea_%28Caribbean_Reef_Squid%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Squid"},{"title":"Pink","blocks":[{"text":"Pink is a pale tint of red or rose, the color of the pink flower. It was first used as a color name in the late 17th century. A combination of pink and white is associated with innocence, whereas a combination of pink and black links to eroticism and seduction."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg/330px-Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pink"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Nautilus_belauensis_profile_%28white_background%29.jpg/500px-Nautilus_belauensis_profile_%28white_background%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Nautilus_belauensis_profile_%28white_background%29.jpg/500px-Nautilus_belauensis_profile_%28white_background%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANautilus_belauensis_profile_(white_background).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/Octopus_vulgaris_Merculiano.jpg/500px-Octopus_vulgaris_Merculiano.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/Octopus_vulgaris_Merculiano.jpg/1280px-Octopus_vulgaris_Merculiano.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/Octopus_vulgaris_Merculiano.jpg/500px-Octopus_vulgaris_Merculiano.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOctopus_vulgaris_Merculiano.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Rhomboteuthis_lehmani_%28cropped%29.jpg/250px-Rhomboteuthis_lehmani_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Rhomboteuthis_lehmani_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Rhomboteuthis_lehmani_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.w